## Purchase history (done)

- Entity `AuthorizationEvent` (`authorization_events`): id, card id, amount, approved, decline reason, created at. Registered in `persistence.xml`.
- `AuthorizationService.authorize` inserts the event in the same transaction as the card update, after the card is found. Missing card: no row. Optimistic lock rollback rolls the event back too.
- `AuthorizationService.recentPurchases()` returns the latest 20 rows for the back office, with masked numbers only.
- `office/cards.xhtml` shows When, Card, Amount, Result, Reason. Trace records the insert on teller purchases and the select on the back office page.
- `CardService.deleteAllCards()` also deletes authorization events (nightly demo reset).

## Login decision (do not "fix" this)

The spec's Phase 4 line says "Jakarta Security". This slice uses a **servlet, a filter, and an HTTP session** instead, so the trace can record the real steps (the spec's own login example: filter, servlet, hash check, session cookie).

- `StaffPassword` stores only the SHA-256 of `demo` (`2a97516c354b68848cdbd8f54a226a0a55b21ed138e207ad6c5cbb9c00aa5aea`). Compare with `MessageDigest.isEqual`. The plain password lives in `StaffSession.DEMO_PASSWORD` for the pages that show the demo account.
- `StaffGateFilter` (`/*`): paths `/office` and `/office/*` need session attribute `demobank.staffUser`. Missing session redirects to `/login`. For those paths it calls `RequestTrace.start()`. For every other path it sets request attribute `demobank.gateNote` and does **not** start the trace (the servlet starts it).
- `LoginServlet` `POST /login` starts the trace, reads the gate note, checks the hash, calls `changeSessionId()`, stores the user, saves the finished step list on the session as `demobank.loginTrace`, redirects to `/office/cards.xhtml`.
- `OfficeBean.getTraceSteps()` prepends that login list **once**, then removes it, then appends `RequestTrace.finish()`. It caches the list. Calling finish twice yields an empty second list.
- `LogoutServlet` is `POST /logout` only.
- Teller, concurrency, home, hello, css, and js stay public.

Do not replace this with container form login unless he asks. A later Learn page can contrast session login with Jakarta Security.

## How the trace works

`com.demobank.trace.RequestTrace` is a `ThreadLocal` list: `start`, `add(layer, title, detail)`, `finish`.

- Teller: `TellerServlet` starts it, JSP reads `traceSteps`.
- Login POST: `LoginServlet` starts it.
- Back office: the filter starts it. `OfficeBean` finishes it at render time. The trace panel is **last** on `cards.xhtml` so card queries are recorded before `finish()`.
- `JpaSupport.inTransaction` adds Begin transaction, Commit, or Rollback. It also calls `SchemaPatches.applyIfNeeded`.
- Layers already styled in `teller.css`: Browser, Filter, Servlet, JSF, EJB, Domain, JPA. New layers need a `.trace-layer-Name` class or they look plain.
- `add` does nothing if `start` was not called. Office actions must run on a request the filter already started.

## Code map

Package `com.demobank`.

| Package | Role |
|---|---|
| `domain` | Rules only. No JPA. `Card` has no setters for balance or status. `authorize`, `freeze`, `unfreeze`. `CreditCard.changeLimit` only. `DebitCard` spends `balance`. `CreditCard` spends against `creditLimit` and tracks `amountUsed`. `Money` is `BigDecimal`, scale at most 2, never negative, never `double`. |
| `persistence` | `CardEntity` (`cards` table, `@Version`), `AuthorizationEvent` (`authorization_events`), `CardMapper.toDomain` / `applyDomainState` (also writes credit limit), `JpaSupport`, `SchemaBootstrap` (`@Singleton @Startup`), `SchemaPatches`. |
| `service` | `CardService`: issue, `listCards`, `search`, `freeze`, `unfreeze`, `changeCreditLimit`, `deleteAllCards` (also clears events). `AuthorizationService`: pay, event insert, `recentPurchases`, async retry for the lab. `ConcurrencyService`, `UnsafeCardWriter`, `DemoDataResetTimer`. All EJBs use `@TransactionManagement(BEAN)` and `JpaSupport`, not container transactions. `@PersistenceUnit(unitName = "DemoBankPU")`. |
| `web` | Servlets plus `OfficeBean`, `CardSummary`, `PurchaseSummary`. |
| `trace` | `RequestTrace`, `TraceStep` (`getLayer`, `getTitle`, `getDetail`). |

UI:

- JSP: `src/main/webapp/WEB-INF/views/` (`teller.jsp`, `concurrency.jsp`, `login.jsp`). Home is `src/main/webapp/index.jsp`.
- JSF: `src/main/webapp/office/cards.xhtml`. `WEB-INF/faces-config.xml` version 4.0 turns on Faces for `*.xhtml`. Bean is `@Named("office")` `@RequestScoped`. `beans.xml` is `bean-discovery-mode="all"`.
- CSS: `css/demobank.css` (shared chrome: `db-shell`, `db-topbar`, `panel`, `db-btn`, `db-table`, `db-flash`) and `css/teller.css` (trace). Bump the `?v=` on the link when CSS changes. No new hex colours inside JSP if a token in `demobank.css` already fits.
- EL on records: `CardSummary` is a record. Facelets uses `#{card.maskedNumber}` (property), not `getMaskedNumber`. Action methods take `String` ids because the page passes `#{card.id}`.
- Credit limit field: `#{office.limitDrafts[card.id]}`. The map is `Map<Object, String>` because EL may use a `UUID` as the key. `draftLimit` matches both the string and `toString()` of the key.

Database: H2 file `jdbc:h2:file:${user.home}/.demobank/demobank`, user `sa`, password `sa`. Not a WildFly datasource. See `docs/DATABASE.md`.

